  4560	/// **6.4-3d (2026-05-29):** map a worker spawn/handshake [`ql_udf::UdfError`] to
  4561	/// a napi `[code] message` error. Only the startup variants are reachable from
  4562	/// `ProcessWorker::ensure_started` (a missing interpreter / worker death during
  4563	/// startup → `WorkerDied`; an incompatible protocol → `Handshake`). A per-call
  4564	/// dispatch failure is NOT routed here — that surfaces as a cell error value +
  4565	/// a `CellDiagnostic`, never a JS exception.
  4566	fn udf_spawn_error_to_napi(e: ql_udf::UdfError) -> Error {
  4567	    match e {
  4568	        ql_udf::UdfError::Handshake { .. } => Error::from_reason(format!("[worker_handshake] {e}")),
  4569	        other => Error::from_reason(format!("[worker_spawn_failed] {other}")),
  4570	    }
  5110	    /// **6.4-3d (2026-05-29):** attach an out-of-process Python-UDF worker to
  5111	    /// this session, built from `config` (a trusted-workspace `ProcessWorker`).
  5112	    /// The worker is spawned + handshaked EAGERLY here (fail-loud) so a missing
  5113	    /// interpreter / protocol mismatch surfaces NOW as a clear error, not later
  5114	    /// as a silent `#CALC!` on the first `=MYUDF(..)`. After injecting, the IDE
  5115	    /// should call `recalcAll` so existing UDF cells pick up the worker — a UDF
  5116	    /// cell computed before injection is a clean `#CALC!` that `recalcDirty`
  5117	    /// will NOT heal (see engine `WorkbookSession::set_udf_worker`). Calling
  5118	    /// again REPLACES the worker (the prior one is dropped → its child killed).
  5119	    ///
  5120	    /// **Errors (Appendix A):**
  5121	    /// - `[worker_spawn_failed]` — the interpreter could not be launched / the
  5122	    ///   worker died during startup (python not found, import error, …).
  5123	    /// - `[worker_handshake]` — the worker reported an incompatible protocol
  5124	    ///   version.
  5125	    /// - `[bad_argument]` — `handshakeTimeoutMs` is negative / non-finite / above
  5126	    ///   the 10-minute cap.
