   318	 *
   319	 * Incremental counterpart to {@link workbookSnapshot}.  Given the
   320	 * `lastSeenVersion` token the caller captured from a prior reply's
   321	 * `version` field (either a {@link WorkbookSnapshotJson.version} or a
   322	 * previous {@link WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson.version}), the engine
   323	 * returns ONLY the cells / sheets / formats that changed since then --
   324	 * 228x faster than a full snapshot at 100 new cells (V3.6.0.8.4 bench).
   325	 *
   326	 * **Two-call protocol** (see the napi docstring on
   327	 * {@link CollabSessionInstance.workbookSnapshotDelta} for the full
   328	 * contract): the FIRST acquisition for a session must come from
   329	 * `workbookSnapshot()` (to seed the engine cache + capture a version);
   330	 * subsequent acquisitions call this.  When the engine cannot produce a
   331	 * delta it returns `fullRebuildRequired=true` (cache miss / staleness /
   332	 * rename / malformed version) and the caller MUST re-fetch via
   333	 * `workbookSnapshot()`.  `fullRebuildRequired` is an explicit, designed
   334	 * protocol signal -- NOT an error to swallow.
   335	 *
   336	 * **`lastSeenVersion` MUST be a real captured `Buffer`** (never
   337	 * `undefined`): the seed path uses `workbookSnapshot()` instead of
   338	 * passing an empty/absent token here.  See
   339	 * `CellGridPanel.acquireWorkbookSnapshot` for the orchestration.
   340	 *
   341	 * Single-line indirection mirrors `workbookSnapshot` for API surface
   342	 * stability across future engine signature changes.
   343	 */
   344	export function workbookSnapshotDelta(
   345		session: CollabSessionInstance,
   346		lastSeenVersion: Buffer,
   347	): WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson {
