   865	    ///    recompute appends NO ops (it must not pollute the log we just
   866	    ///    re-materialized FROM, nor feed the UndoManager a spurious commit).
   867	    ///    Structural recompute failures surface as `CellDiagnostic` events
   868	    ///    (never silently dropped), mirroring `run_recalc`. NOTE: this does NOT
   869	    ///    create an operation-registry entry / `Busy` transition — undo/redo are
   870	    ///    fast synchronous re-derivations, not user-cancellable long ops; the
   871	    ///    op-registry is the shape the out-of-process 6.4/6.5 paths reuse, and a
   872	    ///    re-materialization is internal bookkeeping, not a recalc command.
   873	    /// 4. `bump_epoch` so the next `snapshot_delta` from any pre-undo token
   874	    ///    returns `full_rebuild_required` (`EpochMismatch`) — the wholesale
   875	    ///    rebuild is not incrementally delta-expressible. The token thus changes
   876	    ///    after every consumed undo/redo.
