/bin/zsh -lc "sed -n '240,620p' docs/audits/2026-05-29-6-4-3d-step5-audit/engine-delta.diff" in /Users/sanzhar/Documents/Sanzhar/Sanzhar/quantlab/quantlab-quantbook/quantbook-engine
 succeeded in 0ms:
commit 1e182a2fad3ce67d0b5d75bb033823cc0224bb96
Author: Sanzhar <sanzhar@Sanzhars-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date:   Fri May 29 13:35:36 2026 +0100

    feat(quantbook): 6.4-3d Step 5 (engine) -- pollEvents napi binding + worker no-stderr robustness
    
    Engine prerequisites for the IDE side of 6.4-3d (Python-UDF worker injection).
    
    - napi `Session.pollEvents(cursor)` + faithful Event/Diagnostic/Severity/
      OperationState/CellAddr/EventPage DTOs. Every `Event` variant is modeled
      (No-Fallbacks: none silently dropped). This is how `Event::CellDiagnostic`
      (the 6.4-3d Step G no-worker/raised/timeout/died sink) reaches the IDE so it
      can render WHY a cell is #CALC!. Cursor BigInt->u64 is fail-loud
      (negative/lossy -> [bad_argument]), mirroring registerFunction's implHandle.
      poll_events has no lifecycle gate (pure ring read) -- documented honestly.
    
    - worker.py main(): crash-proof startup when the host gives the child no usable
      stderr. An embedded host (node/electron -- exactly the IDE setUdfWorker path)
      leaves sys.stderr=None; the prior `os.dup2(sys.stderr.fileno(), 1)` raised
      AttributeError on None.fileno(), the worker exited before HELLO_ACK, and every
      UDF call failed with #CALC!. Now: reserve the protocol channel via the raw
      fd 1, redirect fd 1 to real stderr when usable else os.devnull, never assume
      sys.stdout/stderr are non-None. The 6.4-3b audit only ran the worker under
      cargo (fd2 always valid), so this was never exercised.
    
    - clippy: rewrote the pre-existing handshakeTimeoutMs check to
      `!(0.0..=MAX).contains(&ms)` (rust 1.95 manual_range_contains now fires under
      deny(clippy::all); behavior-identical).
    
    - new node smoke crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_udf_pollevents.mjs:
      pollEvents surfaces the udf_no_worker cell_diagnostic; setUdfWorker spawn-fail
      -> [worker_spawn_failed]; real-python =MYUDF(A1) -> 42 (loud-skip if no pyarrow).
    
    Verified: cargo check --workspace clean; clippy -p ql-bindings-node no new
    warnings; release cdylib (--features test-fixtures) builds; ql-udf process_smoke
    2/2 + ql-exec udf_e2e 1/1 (real python, new worker main()); python self_test
    PASS; node smoke all assertions pass.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

