     1	"""Arrow ⇄ engine-value codec + CALL/RETURN/control payload codecs — the Python
     2	mirror of `ql-udf/src/{codec,payload,control}.rs`. 3.9-compatible; needs `pyarrow`.
     3	
     4	A UDF call's args and result are 2-D grids of spreadsheet values. A value is
     5	encoded across five parallel Arrow columns discriminated by ``kind``:
     6	
     7	    kind     populated column   engine Value
     8	    blank    (none)             Blank
     9	    number   num: float64       Number   (finite only; the Rust decoder rejects NaN/Inf)
    10	    bool     bool: bool         Boolean
    11	    text     str: utf8          Text
    12	    error    err: utf8          Error (by sigil, e.g. "#DIV/0!")
    13	
    14	The grid shape rides in the Arrow **schema metadata** (``rows``/``cols``) so
    15	degenerate shapes round-trip. The Rust decoder validates the EXACT schema (field
    16	names, types, nullability) before trusting positions, so this module MUST emit
    17	that schema precisely: ``kind`` non-null utf8, then nullable ``num``/``str``/
    18	``bool``/``err``.
    19	
    20	Payload framings (the ``payload`` inside a `_frame` envelope):
    21	    CALL    [u64 LE handle][u64 LE call_id][grid IPC bytes]
    22	    RETURN  [u64 LE call_id][grid IPC bytes]
    23	    RAISE   [u64 LE call_id][u32 LE exc_type_len][exc_type utf8][message utf8...]
    24	    HELLO   [u32 LE protocol_version]
    25	    HELLO_ACK [u32 LE protocol_version][u32 LE worker_pid]
