   111	            # The engine's Value::Number invariant is "always finite"; the Rust decoder REJECTS
   112	            # NaN/Inf. Reject here at the source so a UDF returning a non-finite number (or a
   113	            # huge int that overflows float() to inf) surfaces a comprehensible RAISE rather than
   114	            # a cryptic codec error from the far side (6.4-3b audit-fix: python-encode-grid-
   115	            # accepts-nan-inf-cryptic-engine-error).
   116	            n = float(cell)
